# Code owners — review routing for the highest-blast-radius paths.
#
# What this file does and does not do, stated honestly:
#   * GitHub auto-requests review from an owner on any PR touching a matched path.
#   * `main` currently has NO branch protection and NO rulesets, so "Require review from Code
#     Owners" is not in force. Until that is enabled, this file ROUTES review; it does not BLOCK
#     a merge. See docs/standards/engineering.md Part C ("documented but not mechanically enforced").
#
# The governance paths below are R2-or-higher by definition in scripts/classify.sh. Listing them
# here is what makes "the agent cannot lower its own class" a mechanism rather than a promise:
# a change to the classifier, the standard, or the agent instructions routes to the operator.

# Default owner for everything not matched below.
